File: lib/OCP/Robocop/Controller.pm:128-178

In `_on_node_event`, two failure paths return early without touching the OCPNode's `status.phase`/`status.message`:

1. Lines 146-150: missing spec.providerRef -> logs and returns, CR stays Pending
2. Lines 157-160: OCP::Provider->from_cr dies (e.g. "spec.hetzner.tokenSecretRef.name missing" raised in OCP/Provider.pm:59,68,80,108) -> exception propagates to the try/catch in run (line 113), catch only logs to STDOUT

Either way operators see a CR stuck Pending with no `message`, and the only diagnostic is robocop's pod logs.

Fix: on every early-return path, patch the CR with `status.phase = Failed` and `status.message = <the local error>`. The catch in run must do the same.

Repro:
1. Apply an OCPNode with spec.providerRef: nonexistent
2. Observe: CR stays Pending, message unset, robocop logs "Failed to load provider CR nonexistent" silently.
